    <p class="section-index">02 · ABOUT</p>
    <h1 id="page-title">Observing the work before telling its story.</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">I'm Scritshell — a developer trained in Multiplatform Application Development (DAM), working mostly in Kotlin, Java and Python, with Firebase and Supabase for anything that needs a backend.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>SCRITSHELL started as an attempt to collect what I build in one place that could grow with me, instead of staying scattered across repositories.</p>
      <p>The projects in the atlas span a chess app built as a final-year project, small tools written to solve a problem I actually had, and a personal Linux setup tuned over time rather than assembled once. Some are public, some stay private — but each one is real, not a demo built to look good in a portfolio.</p>
      <p>Rhythm isn't just the theme of this site. I play BMS and osu!, stream sessions through a Linux setup I built myself, and that's part of where the pace and precision of this design actually come from.</p>
      <p>Lately I've been moving into cybersecurity — still early, but it's the direction I'm building toward next.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
